# Taskmark project memory

If a Taskmark board exists in the workspace, treat it as the source of truth for planned, in-flight, and done product work.

1. Board location:
   - One git product: `<project>/taskmark/`.
   - Multiple git products: dedicated sibling `<common>-taskmark` repository
     root. Never copy the board into product repos.
   - `REPOS.md` is local-generated and gitignored.
2. Before product work, search for a matching item. Prefer an open task/bug
   that fits; if the work is follow-up on something already shipped, append
   Prompt & feedback on that done leaf. Use `/tkmd-plan` or `/tkmd-save` only
   when nothing fits. Every session that does product work writes a `prompt`
   (and `feedback` when the user replies) row on the chosen leaf — never on
   `epic.md` or `story.md`.
3. Use only `/tkmd-init`, `/tkmd-plan`, `/tkmd-save`, `/tkmd-plan-do`,
   `/tkmd-do`, `/tkmd-shelf`, and `/tkmd-commit`.
4. Creation writes new item files only. Never edit existing parent markdown to
   add links, rollups, logs, people, status, or dates.
5. `/tkmd-do` implements the target, never commits or pushes, never uses an
   `in_progress` stage, and marks each successfully executed leaf `done` before
   stopping. During execution, only those leaf board files may change.
6. `/tkmd-shelf` discards never-implemented work without committing or pushing.
   It writes only eligible task/bug leaves as `status: shelved`; parent markdown
   remains unchanged.
7. `/tkmd-commit` is the only user command that commits.
8. Parent hierarchy, rollups, logs, status, implementers, and lifecycle dates
   are read-time views over descendant leaves.
9. Never create or refresh `INDEX.md`, `SIZING.md`, `VELOCITY.md`, or a board
   `README.md`. Never write a Last synced field or changelog.
